32
00:01:04,938 --> 00:01:07,310
Let's start with the oldest truck on

33
00:01:07,310 --> 00:01:09,420
the list, a truck that was built

34
00:01:09,420 --> 00:01:11,265
for war and became a legend.

35
00:01:11,616 --> 00:01:14,518
Number one is the Dodge Power Wagon.

36
00:01:14,698 --> 00:01:16,225
After World War Two,

37
00:01:16,225 --> 00:01:19,583
Dodge took what it learned building military

38
00:01:19,583 --> 00:01:22,865
trucks and sold a civilian four-wheel drive

39
00:01:22,865 --> 00:01:24,162
truck to farmers,

40
00:01:24,162 --> 00:01:26,529
ranchers and utility companies.

41
00:01:26,709 --> 00:01:27,916
It was tough,

42
00:01:27,916 --> 00:01:31,260
slow, simple and almost unstoppable.

43
00:01:31,440 --> 00:01:33,529
It was built to work in places

44
00:01:33,529 --> 00:01:35,341
where roads did not exist.

45
00:01:35,691 --> 00:01:37,997
The Power Wagon was also one of

46
00:01:37,997 --> 00:01:41,047
the first civilian trucks in America sold

47
00:01:41,047 --> 00:01:44,097
with four-wheel drive from the factory as

48
00:01:44,097 --> 00:01:45,362
its main purpose.

49
00:01:45,542 --> 00:01:47,190
That was rare at the time.

50
00:01:47,370 --> 00:01:49,591
Most pickups were two-wheel drive,

51
00:01:49,591 --> 00:01:51,746
and buyers who needed more had to

52
00:01:51,746 --> 00:01:52,595
convert them.

53
00:01:52,775 --> 00:01:55,344
Dodge built the capability in from the

54
00:01:55,344 --> 00:01:57,846
start, and that made the truck famous

55
00:01:57,846 --> 00:02:00,484
among people who worked in hard places.

56
00:02:00,834 --> 00:02:03,909
For decades, the Power Wagon was exactly

57
00:02:03,909 --> 00:02:05,984
what it was designed to be:

58
00:02:05,984 --> 00:02:06,522
a tool.

59
00:02:06,702 --> 00:02:09,257
Many were worked until they fell apart.

60
00:02:09,437 --> 00:02:11,294
Many were left in fields.

61
00:02:11,474 --> 00:02:13,699
But the ones that survived are now

62
00:02:13,699 --> 00:02:16,316
some of the most valuable classic trucks

63
00:02:16,316 --> 00:02:17,035
in America.

64
00:02:17,215 --> 00:02:21,400
At Barrett-Jackson Scottsdale in January twenty twenty-six,

65
00:02:21,400 --> 00:02:24,591
a nineteen fifty-three Dodge Power Wagon sold

66
00:02:24,591 --> 00:02:27,003
for eighty-eight thousand dollars.

67
00:02:27,353 --> 00:02:28,792
And here is the twist.

68
00:02:28,972 --> 00:02:31,822
That truck was rated by Classic dot

69
00:02:31,822 --> 00:02:34,673
com as original or highly original.

70
00:02:34,853 --> 00:02:37,268
That word matters more than anything else.

71
00:02:37,448 --> 00:02:39,819
A Power Wagon that still has its

72
00:02:39,819 --> 00:02:42,486
factory parts is a piece of history.

73
00:02:42,666 --> 00:02:44,997
One that has been heavily modified can

74
00:02:44,997 --> 00:02:46,407
still be a great truck,

75
00:02:46,407 --> 00:02:48,186
but it is a different kind of

76
00:02:48,186 --> 00:02:50,271
vehicle in the eyes of collectors.

77
00:02:50,620 --> 00:02:52,559
Buying one today takes care.

78
00:02:52,739 --> 00:02:55,284
Many Power Wagons have been restored with

79
00:02:55,284 --> 00:02:56,959
parts from different years,

80
00:02:56,959 --> 00:02:59,441
and some have been converted with modern

81
00:02:59,441 --> 00:02:59,938
engines.

82
00:03:00,118 --> 00:03:01,241
For a collector,

83
00:03:01,241 --> 00:03:05,174
matching numbers, original sheet metal and documentation

84
00:03:05,174 --> 00:03:07,350
can change the value by tens of

85
00:03:07,350 --> 00:03:08,825
thousands of dollars.

86
00:03:09,005 --> 00:03:09,959
For a driver,

87
00:03:09,959 --> 00:03:12,822
a well-built restomod can be the better

88
00:03:12,822 --> 00:03:13,336
choice.

89
00:03:13,516 --> 00:03:15,010
The key is knowing which one you

90
00:03:15,010 --> 00:03:15,710
are paying for.

91
00:03:16,059 --> 00:03:18,525
Why did the Power Wagon become a

92
00:03:18,525 --> 00:03:19,450
collectible?

93
00:03:19,630 --> 00:03:21,139
Because it has a story.

94
00:03:21,319 --> 00:03:23,345
It connects to World War Two,

95
00:03:23,345 --> 00:03:25,510
to the farms and ranches of the

96
00:03:25,510 --> 00:03:27,885
post-war years, and to a time when

97
00:03:27,885 --> 00:03:29,701
trucks were built to last.

98
00:03:29,881 --> 00:03:31,867
Collectors do not just buy metal.

99
00:03:32,047 --> 00:03:33,475
They buy stories.

100
00:03:33,655 --> 00:03:35,568
And the Power Wagon has one of

101
00:03:35,568 --> 00:03:37,799
the best in American truck history.

102
00:03:38,150 --> 00:03:39,450
And the name lives on.

103
00:03:39,630 --> 00:03:42,797
Ram still sells a Power Wagon version

104
00:03:42,797 --> 00:03:44,936
of its heavy-duty pickup,

105
00:03:44,936 --> 00:03:46,991
built for off-road work.

106
00:03:47,171 --> 00:03:49,882
When a modern company keeps reusing a

107
00:03:49,882 --> 00:03:51,129
name for decades,

108
00:03:51,129 --> 00:03:53,621
it keeps the original truck in the

109
00:03:53,621 --> 00:03:54,427
public eye.

110
00:03:54,607 --> 00:03:56,962
That helps the old trucks hold their

111
00:03:56,962 --> 00:03:59,840
value, because every new Power Wagon reminds

112
00:03:59,840 --> 00:04:02,130
buyers of where the name came from.

113
00:04:02,480 --> 00:04:04,850
Number two is a truck that most

114
00:04:04,850 --> 00:04:07,832
people never imagined as a collectible.

115
00:04:08,012 --> 00:04:12,400
The nineteen eighty-four to nineteen eighty-eight Toyota

116
00:04:12,400 --> 00:04:13,968
Pickup four by four,

117
00:04:13,968 --> 00:04:15,848
especially the S R five.

118
00:04:16,028 --> 00:04:18,231
For years, it was just a used

119
00:04:18,231 --> 00:04:18,687
truck.

120
00:04:18,867 --> 00:04:22,664
Cheap, tough, and famous for running forever.

121
00:04:22,844 --> 00:04:24,522
People drove them hard,

122
00:04:24,522 --> 00:04:26,346
lifted them, rusted them,

123
00:04:26,346 --> 00:04:28,680
and sold them for a few thousand

124
00:04:28,680 --> 00:04:29,264
dollars.

125
00:04:29,614 --> 00:04:32,267
Then Hagerty named it a Bull Market

126
00:04:32,267 --> 00:04:35,147
pick, its list of vehicles expected to

127
00:04:35,147 --> 00:04:36,208
rise in value.

128
00:04:36,388 --> 00:04:37,919
According to Hagerty,

129
00:04:37,919 --> 00:04:40,034
a number two condition truck,

130
00:04:40,034 --> 00:04:43,825
meaning excellent, was valued at twenty-two thousand

131
00:04:43,825 --> 00:04:45,430
seven hundred dollars,

132
00:04:45,430 --> 00:04:46,669
and a number one,

133
00:04:46,669 --> 00:04:50,169
concours, at thirty-four thousand eight hundred.

134
00:04:50,349 --> 00:04:51,839
Hagerty wrote that,

135
00:04:51,839 --> 00:04:54,506
long considered just a used truck,

136
00:04:54,506 --> 00:04:58,035
it had finally achieved collector car status.

137
00:04:58,385 --> 00:04:59,950
According to Hagerty,

138
00:04:59,950 --> 00:05:03,378
boomers still own forty-three percent of these

139
00:05:03,378 --> 00:05:03,899
trucks.

140
00:05:04,079 --> 00:05:06,657
And a nearly equal third of insurance

141
00:05:06,657 --> 00:05:08,398
quotes come from boomers,

142
00:05:08,398 --> 00:05:09,931
Gen X and millennials.

143
00:05:10,111 --> 00:05:11,318
That is unusual.

144
00:05:11,498 --> 00:05:15,016
Most collectibles are dominated by one generation.

145
00:05:15,196 --> 00:05:18,752
The Toyota pickup appeals to almost everyone,

146
00:05:18,752 --> 00:05:21,597
which is one reason its future looks

147
00:05:21,597 --> 00:05:22,150
strong.

148
00:05:22,501 --> 00:05:23,952
Here is the twist.

149
00:05:24,132 --> 00:05:26,875
Hagerty said the number of these trucks

150
00:05:26,875 --> 00:05:30,111
on its insurance policies had quadrupled since

151
00:05:30,111 --> 00:05:31,307
twenty seventeen.

152
00:05:31,487 --> 00:05:34,288
And collectors under forty more than doubled

153
00:05:34,288 --> 00:05:37,090
their ownership share since twenty nineteen,

154
00:05:37,090 --> 00:05:39,509
from seven percent to sixteen percent.

155
00:05:39,689 --> 00:05:42,952
Young collectors are not buying old Ferraris.

156
00:05:43,132 --> 00:05:45,411
They are buying the Toyota truck they

157
00:05:45,411 --> 00:05:47,321
saw in movies and on the street

158
00:05:47,321 --> 00:05:48,554
when they were kids.

159
00:05:48,904 --> 00:05:50,761
Why does that matter for buyers?

160
00:05:50,941 --> 00:05:54,271
Because demand from younger collectors tends to

161
00:05:54,271 --> 00:05:55,121
last longer.

162
00:05:55,301 --> 00:05:57,308
They will be in the market for

163
00:05:57,308 --> 00:05:57,843
decades.

164
00:05:58,023 --> 00:06:02,238
The Toyota pickup's mechanical simplicity also helps.

165
00:06:02,418 --> 00:06:03,847
It is easy to fix,

166
00:06:03,847 --> 00:06:05,435
parts are available,

167
00:06:05,435 --> 00:06:07,103
and it can be driven,

168
00:06:07,103 --> 00:06:08,374
not just stored.

169
00:06:08,554 --> 00:06:10,814
Collectibles that can be used tend to

170
00:06:10,814 --> 00:06:12,280
keep a wider buyer pool.

171
00:06:12,631 --> 00:06:14,268
And there is an irony here.

172
00:06:14,448 --> 00:06:17,787
Toyota's newer pickups also have a reputation

173
00:06:17,787 --> 00:06:19,123
for holding value,

174
00:06:19,123 --> 00:06:21,572
which is one reason the Tacoma is

175
00:06:21,572 --> 00:06:22,389
so popular.

176
00:06:22,569 --> 00:06:24,453
According to Pedal Commander,

177
00:06:24,453 --> 00:06:27,182
it sold two hundred seventy-four thousand,

178
00:06:27,182 --> 00:06:30,626
six hundred thirty-eight units in twenty twenty-five.

179
00:06:30,806 --> 00:06:33,455
The reputation the old truck built is

180
00:06:33,455 --> 00:06:36,391
still selling new ones forty years later.

181
00:06:36,741 --> 00:06:38,955
Number three is a truck that is

182
00:06:38,955 --> 00:06:41,312
becoming a collectible right now,

183
00:06:41,312 --> 00:06:42,813
