184
00:06:42,993 --> 00:06:46,737
The nineteen eighty to nineteen eighty-six Ford

185
00:06:46,737 --> 00:06:49,366
F-Series, nicknamed the Bullnose.

186
00:06:49,546 --> 00:06:51,114
According to Hagerty,

187
00:06:51,114 --> 00:06:54,025
as reported by Ford Authority in August

188
00:06:54,025 --> 00:06:57,608
twenty twenty-six, it rose thirty-two percent in

189
00:06:57,608 --> 00:07:00,370
value in the second quarter of twenty

190
00:07:00,370 --> 00:07:01,191
twenty-six.

191
00:07:01,371 --> 00:07:03,279
That made it one of the biggest

192
00:07:03,279 --> 00:07:05,679
gainers among all collectible vehicles.

193
00:07:06,029 --> 00:07:07,445
Here is the twist.

194
00:07:07,625 --> 00:07:10,393
Hagerty said the jump was largely driven

195
00:07:10,393 --> 00:07:13,091
by heavy-duty models catching up to the

196
00:07:13,091 --> 00:07:14,475
lighter duty models.

197
00:07:14,655 --> 00:07:18,671
The F-two-fifty and F-three-fifty work trucks,

198
00:07:18,671 --> 00:07:20,067
once worth less,

199
00:07:20,067 --> 00:07:23,734
are now being valued like the F-one-fifty.

200
00:07:23,914 --> 00:07:26,533
And Hagerty noted a notable uptick in

201
00:07:26,533 --> 00:07:29,011
activity being led by the F-Series.

202
00:07:29,191 --> 00:07:30,741
More people are looking,

203
00:07:30,741 --> 00:07:33,777
which usually comes before prices rise further.

204
00:07:34,127 --> 00:07:35,416
At the same time,

205
00:07:35,416 --> 00:07:37,919
the first-generation Ford Bronco,

206
00:07:37,919 --> 00:07:39,512
a famous collectible,

207
00:07:39,512 --> 00:07:42,166
shed twelve percent of its value in

208
00:07:42,166 --> 00:07:43,456
the same quarter,

209
00:07:43,456 --> 00:07:45,655
according to the same report.

210
00:07:45,835 --> 00:07:49,040
And the earliest F-Series pickups had softened.

211
00:07:49,220 --> 00:07:50,671
So the money is moving.

212
00:07:50,851 --> 00:07:53,460
Collectors are leaving some famous names and

213
00:07:53,460 --> 00:07:55,832
moving into trucks that were overlooked.

214
00:07:56,012 --> 00:07:57,923
That is how a truck becomes a

215
00:07:57,923 --> 00:08:00,690
collectible: when the market discovers it.

216
00:08:01,041 --> 00:08:03,140
Here is what that means for anyone

217
00:08:03,140 --> 00:08:03,943
who owns one.

218
00:08:04,123 --> 00:08:06,670
If you have a Bullnose F-Series sitting

219
00:08:06,670 --> 00:08:08,499
in a barn or behind a house,

220
00:08:08,499 --> 00:08:10,524
do not sell it as scrap without

221
00:08:10,524 --> 00:08:12,157
checking its value first.

222
00:08:12,337 --> 00:08:13,549
Look at the cab,

223
00:08:13,549 --> 00:08:15,669
the frame and the paperwork.

224
00:08:15,849 --> 00:08:18,104
A truck that seems worthless to you

225
00:08:18,104 --> 00:08:20,295
may be exactly what a collector is

226
00:08:20,295 --> 00:08:21,712
looking for right now.

227
00:08:22,063 --> 00:08:25,516
The Bullnose has something many collectibles do

228
00:08:25,516 --> 00:08:27,647
not: huge production numbers.

229
00:08:27,827 --> 00:08:31,537
The F-Series has been America's best-selling truck

230
00:08:31,537 --> 00:08:33,689
since nineteen seventy-seven,

231
00:08:33,689 --> 00:08:35,025
according to Ford.

232
00:08:35,205 --> 00:08:36,842
Millions were built.

233
00:08:37,022 --> 00:08:38,740
But most were worked to death.

234
00:08:38,920 --> 00:08:42,582
Clean, rust-free, original examples are much rarer

235
00:08:42,582 --> 00:08:45,218
than the production numbers suggest,

236
00:08:45,218 --> 00:08:47,489
and that is where the value is.

237
00:08:47,839 --> 00:08:49,503
So what is the best way to

238
00:08:49,503 --> 00:08:52,192
buy a Bullnose before prices rise further?

239
00:08:52,372 --> 00:08:56,596
Look for heavy-duty trucks with simple specifications

240
00:08:56,596 --> 00:08:57,951
and solid frames,

241
00:08:57,951 --> 00:09:01,139
since Hagerty says those are catching up

242
00:09:01,139 --> 00:09:01,776
fastest.

243
00:09:01,956 --> 00:09:04,454
Avoid trucks with major rust in the

244
00:09:04,454 --> 00:09:06,096
cab corners and floors,

245
00:09:06,096 --> 00:09:08,808
because repairs can cost more than the

246
00:09:08,808 --> 00:09:09,236
truck.

247
00:09:09,416 --> 00:09:12,504
And buy with documentation whenever possible.

248
