The money went to the National Forest

398
00:15:12,810 --> 00:15:14,789
Foundation and Outward Bound.

399
00:15:14,969 --> 00:15:16,185
It was a new S U V

400
00:15:16,185 --> 00:15:19,293
with an original price of sixty-eight thousand

401
00:15:19,293 --> 00:15:21,726
five hundred dollars before options.

402
00:15:22,076 --> 00:15:24,359
In September twenty twenty-six,

403
00:15:24,359 --> 00:15:26,348
according to autoevolution,

404
00:15:26,348 --> 00:15:29,000
the same vehicle sold again on Bring

405
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:31,873
a Trailer, with just ninety-nine miles,

406
00:15:31,873 --> 00:15:34,673
for one hundred five thousand dollars.

407
00:15:34,853 --> 00:15:36,570
That is less than a third of

408
00:15:36,570 --> 00:15:37,674
its charity price.

409
00:15:37,854 --> 00:15:40,437
A charity auction is not a market

410
00:15:40,437 --> 00:15:40,907
price.

411
00:15:41,087 --> 00:15:43,795
People pay extra because the money goes

412
00:15:43,795 --> 00:15:44,905
to a good cause,

413
00:15:44,905 --> 00:15:47,474
not because the vehicle is worth that

414
00:15:47,474 --> 00:15:47,821
much.

415
00:15:48,171 --> 00:15:50,492
This is the most important lesson in

416
00:15:50,492 --> 00:15:51,201
this video.

417
00:15:51,381 --> 00:15:53,972
A vehicle does not become a collectible

418
00:15:53,972 --> 00:15:56,297
because a company calls it limited,

419
00:15:56,297 --> 00:15:58,622
or because a first example sold for

420
00:15:58,622 --> 00:15:59,752
a headline price.

421
00:15:59,932 --> 00:16:02,470
It becomes a collectible over years,

422
00:16:02,470 --> 00:16:05,361
when demand from real buyers grows faster

423
00:16:05,361 --> 00:16:07,687
than the supply of good examples.

424
00:16:07,867 --> 00:16:09,152
The Power Wagon,

425
00:16:09,152 --> 00:16:12,124
the Toyota and the Lightning all took

426
00:16:12,124 --> 00:16:12,767
decades.

427
00:16:13,117 --> 00:16:15,230
And sometimes values fall.

428
00:16:15,410 --> 00:16:17,639
The first-generation Bronco,

429
00:16:17,639 --> 00:16:20,982
one of the most celebrated collectibles of

430
00:16:20,982 --> 00:16:22,255
the last decade,

431
00:16:22,255 --> 00:16:25,360
lost twelve percent in a single quarter

432
00:16:25,360 --> 00:16:27,031
of twenty twenty-six.

433
00:16:27,211 --> 00:16:29,974
Even real collectibles go through cycles.

434
00:16:30,154 --> 00:16:31,947
Anyone who buys at the top of

435
00:16:31,947 --> 00:16:33,678
a wave can wait years to get

436
00:16:33,678 --> 00:16:34,729
their money back.

437
00:16:35,079 --> 00:16:37,007
There is a lesson for new truck

438
00:16:37,007 --> 00:16:37,691
buyers too.

439
00:16:37,871 --> 00:16:39,761
When a dealer tells you a new

440
00:16:39,761 --> 00:16:41,717
truck is a future collectible,

441
00:16:41,717 --> 00:16:42,434
be careful.

442
00:16:42,614 --> 00:16:45,327
Many limited editions are built in large

443
00:16:45,327 --> 00:16:48,109
numbers, and most new vehicles lose value

444
00:16:48,109 --> 00:16:49,533
in their first years.

445
00:16:49,713 --> 00:16:52,559
The Bronco Raptor number zero zero zero

446
00:16:52,559 --> 00:16:54,310
one is the extreme case,

447
00:16:54,310 --> 00:16:57,009
but the rule applies to every special

448
00:16:57,009 --> 00:16:58,177
edition sticker.

449
00:16:58,527 --> 00:17:00,691
Here is another way to spot a

450
00:17:00,691 --> 00:17:04,048
future collectible: look at insurance quotes,

451
00:17:04,048 --> 00:17:05,168
not just sales.

452
00:17:05,348 --> 00:17:08,829
Hagerty tracks which vehicles people are asking

453
00:17:08,829 --> 00:17:10,607
to insure, by age group.

454
00:17:10,787 --> 00:17:14,590
When quote activity rises among younger buyers,

455
00:17:14,590 --> 00:17:16,209
values often follow.

456
00:17:16,389 --> 00:17:18,963
That is exactly what happened with the

457
00:17:18,963 --> 00:17:21,401
Toyota pickup and the Bullnose Ford,

458
00:17:21,401 --> 00:17:23,298
and it is a signal any buyer

459
00:17:23,298 --> 00:17:26,211
can watch through published market reports.

460
00:17:26,561 --> 00:17:28,604
And look at what gets reproduced.

461
00:17:28,784 --> 00:17:32,159
When aftermarket companies start making new body

462
00:17:32,159 --> 00:17:34,902
panels, interiors and trim for a truck,

463
00:17:34,902 --> 00:17:37,363
it means there are enough owners to

464
00:17:37,363 --> 00:17:38,699
support a business.

465
00:17:38,879 --> 00:17:42,077
That makes restoration easier and keeps more

466
00:17:42,077 --> 00:17:45,420
trucks alive, which grows the community around

467
00:17:45,420 --> 00:17:46,147
the model.

468
00:17:46,327 --> 00:17:48,505
A healthy parts market is one of

469
00:17:48,505 --> 00:17:51,296
the quiet signs of a lasting collectible.

470
00:17:51,646 --> 00:17:54,727
Finally, condition is king at every level

471
00:17:54,727 --> 00:17:55,779
of the market.

472
00:17:55,959 --> 00:17:57,936
In every example in this video,

473
00:17:57,936 --> 00:18:00,041
the best trucks sold for far more

474
00:18:00,041 --> 00:18:01,125
than the average.

475
00:18:01,305 --> 00:18:03,103
A rough Power Wagon,

476
00:18:03,103 --> 00:18:06,158
Syclone or Lightning is a project.

477
00:18:06,338 --> 00:18:09,786
A clean, documented one is an asset.

478
00:18:09,966 --> 00:18:10,696
If you can,

479
00:18:10,696 --> 00:18:13,015
buy the best example you can afford

480
00:18:13,015 --> 00:18:15,335
instead of the cheapest one you can

481
00:18:15,335 --> 00:18:15,667
find.

482
00:18:16,017 --> 00:18:18,008
So what turns a truck into a

483
00:18:18,008 --> 00:18:18,861
collectible?

484
00:18:19,041 --> 00:18:20,283
Five things.

485
00:18:20,463 --> 00:18:23,345
A story, like the Power Wagon's link

486
00:18:23,345 --> 00:18:24,225
to the war.

487
00:18:24,405 --> 00:18:27,251
Nostalgia, like the Toyota and the Lightning

488
00:18:27,251 --> 00:18:29,386
for people who grew up with them.

489
00:18:29,566 --> 00:18:33,107
Survivors, because most examples were used up.

490
00:18:33,287 --> 00:18:35,992
Simplicity, so they can be kept running.

491
00:18:36,172 --> 00:18:38,590
And a buyer group that is growing,

492
00:18:38,590 --> 00:18:39,585
not shrinking.

493
00:18:39,935 --> 00:18:41,657
And the twist in that list is

494
00:18:41,657 --> 00:18:44,033
that none of these trucks were expensive

495
00:18:44,033 --> 00:18:44,567
when new.

496
00:18:44,747 --> 00:18:46,361
They were work trucks,

497
00:18:46,361 --> 00:18:49,588
cheap trucks, or oddball performance trucks.

498
00:18:49,768 --> 00:18:52,400
The collectibles of the future are probably

499
00:18:52,400 --> 00:18:54,298
sitting in driveways right now,

500
00:18:54,298 --> 00:18:55,583
being used every day,

501
00:18:55,583 --> 00:18:57,419
and their owners have no idea.

502
00:18:57,770 --> 00:18:59,709
A final point about time.

503
00:18:59,889 --> 00:19:02,479
Every truck on this list spent years

504
00:19:02,479 --> 00:19:05,717
being ignored before it became a collectible.

505
00:19:05,897 --> 00:19:08,472
The Power Wagon was a work truck

506
00:19:08,472 --> 00:19:09,438
for decades.

507
00:19:09,618 --> 00:19:12,538
The Toyota was a cheap used truck

508
00:19:12,538 --> 00:19:13,600
for decades.

509
00:19:13,780 --> 00:19:16,172
If you are buying to profit,

510
00:19:16,172 --> 00:19:17,624
think in decades,

511
00:19:17,624 --> 00:19:18,563
not months.

512
00:19:18,743 --> 00:19:20,360
If you are buying for fun,

513
00:19:20,360 --> 00:19:22,412
the clock does not matter at all.

514
00:19:22,762 --> 00:19:23,958
And enjoy the truck.

515
00:19:24,138 --> 00:19:27,245
Collectible trucks are meant to be driven,

516
00:19:27,245 --> 00:19:28,503
shown and shared.

517
00:19:28,683 --> 00:19:31,166
Many owners find that the people they

518
00:19:31,166 --> 00:19:33,113
meet at shows and on the road

519
00:19:33,113 --> 00:19:35,730
are worth more than any price increase.

520
00:19:35,910 --> 00:19:38,287
A truck that brings you joy every

521
00:19:38,287 --> 00:19:40,952
weekend is already a good investment,

522
00:19:40,952 --> 00:19:43,329
whatever the auction results say.

523
00:19:43,679 --> 00:19:45,110
So if you want to buy a

524
00:19:45,110 --> 00:19:47,662
collectible truck in twenty twenty-seven,

525
00:19:47,662 --> 00:19:49,031
here is what to check.

526
00:19:49,211 --> 00:19:51,057
First, originality.

527
00:19:51,237 --> 00:19:53,096
Original engine, paint,

528
00:19:53,096 --> 00:19:56,329
interior and documents can be worth more

529
00:19:56,329 --> 00:19:57,704
than any upgrade.

530
00:19:57,884 --> 00:19:59,521
Second, the trend.

531
00:19:59,701 --> 00:20:02,068
Look at values over three to five

532
00:20:02,068 --> 00:20:03,718
years, not one auction.

533
00:20:03,898 --> 00:20:05,674
Third, who is buying.

534
00:20:05,854 --> 00:20:08,889
A truck loved by younger collectors usually

535
00:20:08,889 --> 00:20:10,301
has a longer future.

536
00:20:10,651 --> 00:20:13,890
Fourth, ignore charity and first-of prices.

537
00:20:14,070 --> 00:20:15,301
They are not the market.

538
00:20:15,481 --> 00:20:17,875
And fifth, count the full cost:

539
00:20:17,875 --> 00:20:21,505
storage, insurance, maintenance and the time it

540
00:20:21,505 --> 00:20:22,586
takes to sell.

541
00:20:22,766 --> 00:20:25,539
A collectible truck is a passion first

542
00:20:25,539 --> 00:20:27,363
and an investment second.

543
00:20:27,543 --> 00:20:30,054
Buy the one you will enjoy owning,

544
00:20:30,054 --> 00:20:32,269
even if its value never moves.

545
00:20:32,619 --> 00:20:34,418
One last practical tip.

546
00:20:34,598 --> 00:20:37,590
Get a valuation from an independent source

547
00:20:37,590 --> 00:20:40,298
before you buy or insure a collectible

548
00:20:40,298 --> 00:20:42,435
truck, and keep every receipt.

549
00:20:42,615 --> 00:20:45,181
A documented history is one of the

550
00:20:45,181 --> 00:20:47,596
easiest ways to add value to any

551
00:20:47,596 --> 00:20:48,350
old truck.

552
00:20:48,530 --> 00:20:50,282
When it is time to sell,

553
00:20:50,282 --> 00:20:52,618
buyers pay more for a truck they

554
00:20:52,618 --> 00:20:53,348
can trust.

555
00:20:53,699 --> 00:20:55,619
We put the full checklist,

556
00:20:55,619 --> 00:20:58,056
for new, used and classic trucks,

557
